  "source": {
    "title": "Biobizz Nutrient Schedule, EN 2025",
    "url": "https://biobizz.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Nutrient-Schedule-EN-PF-2025.pdf",
    "readAt": "2026-09-22"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The chart's columns are PROPAGATION, GROWTH and WK 1-10, where WK 1 is the first week of flowering. They are laid out here as week 1 (propagation), weeks 2-3 (growth, the column the chart says can last for as long as needed) and weeks 4-11 (WK 1-8), so the flip falls on week 4.",
    "WK 9 is the chart's plain-water week and is kept as week 12 with every figure absent; WK 10 is the harvest and is no feeding week at all.",
    "Fish·Mix is not a row of its own: the chart offers it as a replacement for Bio·Grow in the vegetative phase, and shipping both would dose the can twice.",
    "CalMag is not a row either: the chart gives it only for RO or very soft water, as week ranges rather than per week, so it is something a grower adds to their own grid.",
    "All·Mix is pre-fertilised, which is the whole of the difference: the chart holds Bio·Grow at 1 ml/l throughout and prints no Alg·A·Mic row.",
    "The chart prints no EC: it gives a pH range (6.2-6.5) and nothing a meter could be held against per week, so every week states ecTarget null and the grid draws no EC row."
  ],
